{"duration_api_ms": 61882, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "022639c6-5f80-428d-b08e-e66fbd7a097f", "total_cost_usd": 0.1034447, "usage": {"input_tokens": 98, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 25236, "cache_read_input_tokens": 279647, "output_tokens": 4982, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1546}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 25236, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 8, "output_tokens": 2144, "cache_read_input_tokens": 36733, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 456, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 456}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": {"inputTokens": 98, "outputTokens": 4982, "cacheReadInputTokens": 279647, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 25236, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.1034447, "contextWindow": 200000, "maxOutputTokens": 32000, "thinkingTokens": 1546, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-4-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 23, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "Now I'll create a concise summary of what an implementer needs to know.\n\n---\n\n## Summary: What an Implementer of SPEC.md Needs to Know\n\n### The Three Export Systems\n\n**System A (Ardent)** exports with ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD) and decimal dollar amounts. Descriptions can contain quoted fields. Reader detects it by banner \"# ARDENT LEDGER EXPORT\".\n\n**System B (Borough)** is plain comma-delimited with no quoting. Critically, its `amount` column is in **integer cents**, not dollars—a value of 25440 means $254.40. Dates are ISO. Every row repeats 'B' in the first column. Detected by header starting with \"sys,doc_no,value_date\".\n\n**System C (Calder)** has a banner line and trailer row counting records. Dates are **DD/MM/YYYY** (day-first, unlike the other two). Amounts are decimal dollars. Detected by \"CALDER EXPORT\" banner.\n\nThe three systems' **column names are completely different**: Ardent uses `entry_id`, Borough uses `doc_no`, Calder uses `ref`. Each reader (`parsers/system_a.py`, etc.) returns raw strings keyed by its own column names; the caller determines which system it is and converts to `Record` objects.\n\n### The Record Type\n\nEvery posting becomes a `Record` (in `core/records.py`), holding these fields as normalized types:\n- `record_id` (str, as the source gave it)\n- `source_system` ('A', 'B', or 'C')\n- `date` (`datetime.date`)\n- `account_code` (uppercase)\n- `account_name` (from mapping, or `unknown_account_label` if unmapped)\n- `description` (normalized whitespace)\n- `amount` (`decimal.Decimal` in dollars, negative for refunds)\n\nRecords are sorted by date, then source system, then record ID.\n\n### The Five Commands to Build\n\n**1. `ingest`** merges multiple exports into one normalized CSV. It calls each system's reader, converts rows to Records (parsing dates per-system, converting Borough cents to dollars), looks up account names, sorts everything, writes a CSV with the standard header, and prints a summary line.\n\n**2. `report`** reads the normalized CSV and prints totals. It sums amounts either by account code (ascending) or by month (YYYY-MM, ascending), respecting the `--include-refunds` flag. Totals are rendered with ROUND_HALF_EVEN rounding at the `decimals` setting.\n\n**3. `reconcile`** reads the normalized CSV and finds account/month pairs where the source systems disagree (spread > tolerance). It prints lines for each mismatch and a count at the end.\n\n**4. `validate`** reads raw exports and checks for malformed rows: wrong field count, unparseable dates (per format), non-numeric amounts, or account codes not matching the regex. It logs a WARNING per bad row and exits 0 if all pass, 2 if any reject.\n\n**5. `--config PATH`** is a global option parsed before the subcommand; it overrides the settings file. Settings layer: built-in defaults → `config/settings.toml` → override file. Readers don't call `load_settings()` directly; they pass strings to the command handler, which loads settings once.\n\n### Implementation Checklist\n\n- All amounts in-memory are `Decimal`, never `float`\n- All dates in-memory are `datetime.date`\n- Convert Borough amounts by dividing cents by 100\n- Parse Calder dates as DD/MM/YYYY, not MM/DD\n- Round only at output time, using `Decimal.quantize(..., rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)`\n- Use the logger: `from ledgerkit.log import get_logger; _log = get_logger(__name__)`\n- All output goes through `cli.emit()`, never `print()`\n- Every public function must have full type annotations\n- No new dependencies; standard library only\n- Don't edit `config/` files; the `--config` option handles overrides\n- Follow CONVENTIONS.md: no floats, one logger per module, type hints on public functions", "ttft_ms": 1768, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 63236, "uuid": "dd7a0a89-7ee5-47c0-b40c-154d6184eb21", "ttft_stream_ms": 831, "time_to_request_ms": 151, "first_content_frame_ms": 1125, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 64.6, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/N/haiku/topic-r1-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
