units**, that is, whole cents\" and \"a reader that treats the column as dollars gets numbers a hundred times too large and no error to go with them.\" **Must divide by 100.**\n\nSystem C writes decimal dollars: `386.54`, `284.04`. Directly usable.\n\n**Dates:**\n\nSystem A writes ISO: `2026-01-03`, `2026-02-11`. Standard YYYY-MM-DD, directly parseable.\n\nSystem B writes ISO: `2026-01-07`, `2026-02-04`. Standard YYYY-MM-DD, directly parseable.\n\nSystem C writes **DD/MM/YYYY**: `02/01/2026`, `14/02/2026`. The comment in `system_c.py` warns: \"Read month first and the rows past the twelfth of a month blow up, while the rows on or before it quietly land in the wrong month.\" Looking at the sample, `11/01/2026` is January 11th, not November 1st. **Must parse day-first.**\n\nSo: **Amounts and dates are not directly comparable as written. Borough amounts need ÷100 conversion, and Calder dates need DD/MM/YYYY parsing.** These conversions happen when building each `Record` from the raw reader output, since the caller knows which system it's holding.", "ttft_ms": 9387, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 13487, "uuid": "816f4bbb-bd7c-4aea-a2d3-8186e914ebc5", "ttft_stream_ms": 1108, "time_to_request_ms": 293, "first_content_frame_ms": 1351, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 16.1, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-anatoly/24e92440-efc2-4a14-97c2-ee126ebf0ca1/scratchpad/ab/topic/N/haiku/topic-r1-topic-b", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin", "--resume", "022639c6-5f80-428d-b08e-e66fbd7a097f"]}
